      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When evaluating the stability of a neighborhood for commercial investment, several environmental and community factors can signal decline or instability. These include high crime rates, vacant or dilapidated buildings, low property values, and decreased foot traffic. Additionally, the presence of industrial or commercial sites with hazardous waste, pollution, or health concerns can also be a warning sign. Additionally, gentrification, population decline, and limited community resources can also indicate a neighborhood is on the decline.",
